Z||000000||Smoooooth GT||07-15-2001||10:00 AM||||Thank's for wanting to help me again...lol   <BR>My ? is...  What is the easiest way to remove the front and rear spring's??? <BR>Do I need any*special* tool's to do this other then a set of spring compressor's(sp)??<BR>Thank's for any help I can get on this subject... I tried the search but no real answer's on this removal question...  Thank's Steve....<P>------------------<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG">   <BR>  with a 100-125HP shot of NOS...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||07-15-2001||10:34 AM||||Front Springs:<BR>The only special tool you need is a "pickle fork" to seperate the lower ball joint. <BR>Raise front of car 16".<BR>Remove caliper and rotor.<BR>Remove nut and cotter pin from lower ball joint.<BR>Place floor jack under control arm.<BR>Remove shock and sway bar link.<BR>Seperate the lower ball joint from spindle.<BR>SLOWLY lower control arm with jack. <BR>Once arm is all the way down use large screwdrive or a crowbar to unhook spring from lower arm perch.<BR>To put it back together just reverse the above. You may need to buy a new boot for the ball joint if it gets damaged.<P>Rear springs:<BR>Remove the 2 strut bolts from hub assembly.<BR>Remove the 3 strut mount bolts on top.<BR>The strut comes out as an assembly. If you are replacing springs or strut, You can take the parts to a local shop who can seperate the strut assembly and install the new items.<BR>If using the same strut, It is best to scribe a line so that when you re-install the strut you can get the alignment very close to what it was.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||07-15-2001||10:49 AM||||Thank's...  wow , sound's pretty simple...  I'm putting some lowering spring's on there.... Thank's.. Steve||||reg||1
